{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nice-ashamed-crustacean","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe preserved AWS review-bot clone contains structured code-review telemetry stranded by the intentional tickets-history rewrite. Operational correctness does not require it because Gerrit retains the votes, but the seven REVIEW_RESULT payloads contain audit detail not guaranteed to remain in Gerrit. The operator authorized an exact selective transplant before quiet-window closeout.\n\n## Approach\n\nAt source HEAD 376bc29eadd42f9bb4335f4e365bf53119bb41d3, derive a content-hashed allowlist from the diff against tracking ref 9ffd0f8ed06d458e54192cbc05d4ff391f49a58e. Accept exactly five CREATE, seven REVIEW_RESULT, and nine LINK events. Require every CREATE to be code_review, every sidecar to belong to those five artifacts, and every LINK to be relates_to from an artifact to an existing implementation ticket. Reject ENQUEUE_ENRICH, CLAIM_ENRICH, DONE_ENRICH, any removed comment alias, path collision, or extra event.\n\nUse rebar._store.event_append.batch_write_and_push (src/rebar/_store/event_append.py) against the recreated live review-bot store. That canonical writer validates fully composed events, stages all 21 atomically under the unified ticket lock, commits one path-scoped batch, and uses the normal tickets push/reconvergence path. src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py serializes the supplied event dictionaries without re-deriving timestamp, UUID, author, environment, or signature, preserving the signed source bytes while avoiding any merge of the 399 divergent commits.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo codebase files change. The mutation is limited to the 21 allowlisted event paths, one additive tickets-branch commit, and private off-repository manifest/verification receipts. The preserved source clone remains read-only. All 66 enrichment events, the untracked stale DONE_ENRICH, removed comment material, and divergent git ancestry are excluded.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Preflight: compute the source allowlist and SHA-256 manifest twice; require equal digests, exact type counts, valid artifact ownership/link targets, valid event filenames, and zero target-path collisions at the current authoritative tip.\n- Failure path: run the validator with one excluded enrichment path and require refusal before the canonical writer is called.\n- Rehearsal: apply the exact batch to a disposable clone at the current epoch, then require strict fsck, reducer visibility of five code-review artifacts with seven sidecars and nine links, authorship verification, and a tree delta containing only the 21 paths.\n- Live: revalidate the source and target immediately before batch_write_and_push, capture the exact origin lease, publish through the canonical writer, and verify from a fresh clone. Re-run the 1,520 removed-alias oracle and the Jira cleanup observation to prove non-resurrection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A signed-content manifest identifies exactly 21 source events with counts CREATE=5, REVIEW_RESULT=7, LINK=9 and no enrichment event; checked by two equal SHA-256 calculations recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A disposable current-epoch rehearsal has only the 21-path additive delta and passes strict fsck, reducer, authorship, and link-target checks; the candidate tip and receipt digest are recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The authoritative store contains the five transplanted code-review artifacts, seven structured review results, and nine relates_to links after one canonical batch write; checked from a fresh clone and recorded with the publication OID.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No removed echo material or stale enrichment work is restored; checked by 0/1,520 removed aliases, unchanged Jira cleanup observation, and an authoritative enrichment-state comparison recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The forensic source clone remains at HEAD 376bc29eadd42f9bb4335f4e365bf53119bb41d3 with its untracked DONE_ENRICH preserved; checked by post-operation read-only status recorded on this ticket.","id":"f0d8-b6e4-c2fa-4abd","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["store","audit","code-review","maintenance"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Transplant preserved code-review audit events onto the current tickets epoch"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787798943534275001,"uuid":"74b8ed28-a958-4714-9dbc-9a0a83a7496a"}